From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emaki contributors <emaki@localhost>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Protect session pixels while locked

Copyright (C) 2026 Artur Yakymenko
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

Blank window screencasts in both output and PipeWire redraw callbacks before
accessing the window. Reject direct window screenshots while locked.

Return lock surfaces before session overlays and cached transitions for all
render targets. Keep the focused exit confirmation above the lock.
Skip session xray preparation, suppress drag icons and accept
surface cursors only from the lock client. Output screencasts, screencopy and
portal screenshots then share the lock-screen composition.

Add headless pixel regressions for transitions, session overlays and pointer
surfaces, including a real session-lock client and unlock recovery.

This applies to Locking and Locked. Pixels captured or queued before locking
cannot be revoked; the existing unconfirmed wait for lock surfaces is unchanged.
---
